---
// src/pages/buy-staffy-puppies-for-sale-uk/index.astro — REBUILT from the approved board
// record (data/boards/buy-staffy-puppies-for-sale-uk.json, approved 2026-09-20). Hand-written
// and NOT regenerated by `npm run extract`: the slug is listed in data/facts/rebuilt.json, so
// `migration_parity.py` skips it and `facts_preserved_check.py`, `link_parity_check.py` and
// `verbatim_set_check.py` are its gates instead.
//
// THIS IS THE WHY-US PAGE. Its question is "why you and not somebody else", so every reason on
// it names the test result, the registration, the record or the contract behind it, and NOT
// ONE MONEY FIGURE IS STATED IN ITS PROSE. The migrated £850 to £1,200 band is below the
// locked prices (Known Issue 11, `dropped.prices`) and /blue-staffy-pup-sale-uk/ is the page
// that states the two prices once; /buy-blue-staffy-puppies-uk/ is the listing and owns the
// six dogs. Both are linked from the opening rather than answered a second time here. The
// only sourced figures on the page are the counter strip's three, and all three are derived at
// build from the files they cite rather than copied out of the record.
//
// NO SCHEME MEMBERSHIP, NO LICENCE, NO LIFETIME SUPPORT, NO PERCENTAGE AND NO RATING (the
// two-year guarantee is stated, from data/settings.json `guarantee_label`, answer board q07). The migrated body claimed the Kennel Club Assured Breeder Scheme five times,
// DEFRA approval of itself twice, lifetime support three times and a BVA/RSPCA alignment; no
// file on disk records any of them, and each is logged in the record's `dropped.creds` with
// its reason. DEFRA appears here only as the TRANSPORT wording data/settings.json holds.
//
// WORKING RULE 15 (faithful rewrite). The VERBATIM SET — the migrated H1, every H2/H3
// carrying a target keyword, the first paragraph under each of those headings, the FAQ
// questions and every image alt — is carried WORD FOR WORD, and the carried wording is READ
// OFF THE RECORD (`sections[].heading`, `sections[].verbatim_opening`, the tree nodes' own
// pair, `assets[].alt`) rather than retyped here, so a curly quote cannot drift between the
// record the breeder approved and the page that ships. THE THREE NUMBERS, and which is which:
// the set holds 91 ELEMENTS, `verbatim.changed` holds 47 ROWS, and those rows account for 48
// ELEMENTS — one more than there are rows, because the migrated body printed one opening
// paragraph under two different headings and a single row excuses both readings of it.
// `verbatim_set_check --check` counts ELEMENTS (91 examined / 48 changed / 0 missing) and the
// record holds the rows. THE H1 IS NOT ONE OF THEM: `h1.pick` is variant 0,
// which is the migrated H1 word for word (`h1.verbatim_heading: true`), so the picked H1 and
// the verbatim H1 are one string and no `h1` row is owed. Everything else on the page is
// written fresh, in Lisa Bright's first person, from the record's outline.
//
// WORKING RULE 16. The hero is `H-FS2` (a full-bleed photograph above the copy, the trust
// chips under the lede) and the counter strip is `C-FS2` (ring tiles in a card beside the
// heading, labels under the figures) — the for-sale family's own arrangements, resolved
// through `pickedStyle()` exactly as every other section's pick is, and neither of them one
// /blue-staffy-pup-sale-uk/ or /buy-blue-staffy-puppies-uk/ took. H-FS2's ledge is `chips`, so
// the record's chips are what sits under the lede and the arrangement is what decides that the
// ticks and the figures do not render there; there are no CTA buttons on it (amendment 6a).
//
// SIXTEEN SECTIONS, in the record's order, each mounted in the style `approval.picks` names.
// TWO OF THEM CARRY NO PICK — `compared` and `getting-home` were restored at Task 18b so the
// migrated comparison and delivery headings have a section to stand in (working rule 15), and
// their `options.pick` is null — so they render with no `bl-box` class at all, exactly as
// /blue-staffy-pup-sale-uk/'s close does. `pickedStyle()` is never called for them: an
// invented pick would be an arrangement nobody chose.
//
// THE EMBED IS CARRIED AT ITS ORIGINAL ID (working rule 14, spec §9 amendment 7).
// `g88qOo9C94c` is the one id data/facts records for this page; it is mounted through
// `VideoEmbed` in the record's own `video-why-us` section — directly below the opening, where
// the migrated body had it — and the picked style is S3, the click-to-play facade.
//
// SCHEMA IS WebPage + FAQPage AND NO OFFER (`brief.schema.types`, `offer_model: "none"`).
// WebPage comes from BaseLayout. The listing page owns the six per-puppy Offers and the price
// page owns the AggregateOffer; a third page claiming either would be claiming one sale twice.
//
// H4-H6 ARE WRITTEN HERE, not in the record (amendment 2.1): the approved outline stops at the
// H3 the breeder read. Every ladder sentence traces to the migrated body or to a file under
// data/ (amendment 6f), and the H6 lines all open on the record's own `tuple.h6_prefixes`
// entry, "Reason Note:". Every heading renders through `titleCase()` (amendment 4b) —
// approved wording, site-wide case.
import PageShell from '../../layouts/PageShell.astro';
import Hero from '../../components/kit/Hero.astro';
import CounterStrip from '../../components/kit/CounterStrip.astro';
import TrustStrip, { type TrustItem } from '../../components/kit/TrustStrip.astro';
import VideoEmbed from '../../components/kit/VideoEmbed.astro';
import InfoCard from '../../components/kit/InfoCard.astro';
import PuppyCard from '../../components/kit/PuppyCard.astro';
import Testimonial from '../../components/kit/Testimonial.astro';
import ContactFormKit from '../../components/kit/ContactFormKit.astro';
import Faq from '../../components/kit/Faq.astro';
import { sectionsFromRecord } from '../../lib/sections';
import { pickedStyle } from '../../lib/pickedStyle';
import { bakedAssets } from '../../lib/assets';
import { boxClass } from '../../lib/boardStyles';
import { recordText, countedFigures, sourceKey, ledgeText, numberWord, type LedgeEntry } from '../../lib/recordText';
import { titleCase as T } from '../../lib/headings';
import { loadFaq } from '../../lib/faq';
import { SITE, abs, guaranteeLabel, guaranteeCoverSentence, type PuppyRow } from '../../lib/site';
import { videoObject } from '../../lib/video';
import puppiesJson from '../../../data/puppies.json';
import reviewsJson from '../../../data/reviews.json';
import settings from '../../../data/settings.json';
import healthRecord from '../../../data/boards/blue-staffy-health-uk.json';
import record from '../../../data/boards/buy-staffy-puppies-for-sale-uk.json';

const path = '/buy-staffy-puppies-for-sale-uk/';
// The picked meta variants and H1, BY INDEX from the approval — never retyped here.
const title = record.meta_set.titles[record.approval!.meta!.title];
const description = record.meta_set.descriptions[record.approval!.meta!.description];
const h1 = record.h1.variants[record.approval!.h1];

// The thirteen photographs, by slot, at their ORIGINAL public paths with the alt text the
// record baked (working rule 11; all thirteen alts are thirteen elements of the verbatim set,
// and `why-kc-explained`'s is the one the record repaired — the migrated wording asserted the
// Assured Breeder scheme twice and an alt is page copy). The two optional hero tiles are NOT
// mounted: H-FS2 is a full-bleed photograph and not a mosaic, and both tiles point at files
// this page already renders in their own sections. A missing slot throws at build.
const asset = bakedAssets(record);
const heroPhoto = asset('why-hero');
const norwichPups = asset('why-norwich-pups');
const englishPup = asset('why-english-pup');
const vetCheck = asset('why-vet-check');
const temperament = asset('why-temperament');
const kcExplained = asset('why-kc-explained');
const kcCertified = asset('why-kc-certified');
const healthyPup = asset('why-healthy-pup');
const comparisonGraphic = asset('why-affordable-vs-premium');
const ownerReviews = asset('why-owner-reviews');
const satisfiedOwner = asset('why-satisfied-owner');
const readyNow = asset('why-ready-now');
const localBreeders = asset('why-local-breeders');

// THE SIX PUPPIES, filtered on `status` rather than hard-coded: a puppy leaving the list is a
// data edit, not a page edit. Their card links are the grid's own data and are exempt from
// link parity (amendment 6b). No per-puppy Offer is emitted here — the listing owns them.
const available = (puppiesJson as PuppyRow[]).filter((p) => p.status === 'Available');

// ALL THREE REVIEWS, as a grid. `approval.picks` gives `owners` S3, and S3's own definition
// IS `mode: 'grid'` (src/lib/boardStyles.ts) — `mode` is one of the axes RENDERED_AXES lists
// for the reviews shape, so on this shape the pick decides the count as well as the bed. The
// first build passed `mode="single"` from `approval.notes.owners`, which reads "MODE: single —
// pick S1"; the note and the pick were two answers to one question and THE PICK IS THE
// ANSWER THE BREEDER GAVE. The note has been amended through
// `board_approve.py --reapprove` (spec §9 amendment 11) to say what the pick says, and the
// mode now comes from the StyleDef like every other axis. Every slot is filled, so no
// REVIEW_PLACEHOLDER renders here.
const allReviews = reviewsJson;

// THE FOUR DOCUMENTS THE RECORD'S `promises` SECTION NAMES, passed to the kit strip rather
// than left to its default three. The record's intent says "the four things we can actually
// hand a reader", the paragraph beside the strip lists four, and a strip printing three made
// the section contradict itself. Each of the four is backed on disk, which is the condition
// working rule 9 puts on a credential: KC registration is `data/facts/…json` creds and the
// `whyus-paperwork` FAQ row; the two DNA tests are that file's `tests` and the
// `about-health-tests` row; the veterinary check and the microchip are its `tests` again and
// the `puppy-package` row; and the written puppy purchase contract is the migrated sentence
// data/facts records ("…and a full puppy purchase contract"), the `whyus-paperwork` row, a
// FACT_PHRASE tests/py/test_faq_data.py holds this page to, and the approved H1's own clause.
const PROMISED: TrustItem[] = [
  { t: 'Kennel Club registered', d: 'Registration paperwork for the litter, and both parents’ numbers on request.',
    i: 'M12 2l3 6 6 1-4.5 4.5L18 20l-6-3-6 3 1.5-6.5L3 9l6-1z' },
  // NOT the kit default's wording, which the homepage renders: "Dam and sire DNA tested for
  // L-2-HGA and HC-HSF4; eyes and elbows screened too" would have put a long run on two pages, which is
  // the crossover the dup gate exists to catch (rule 8). Same two tests, this page's sentence.
  { t: 'Two DNA tests', d: 'Both parents screened for L-2-HGA and HC-HSF4 before a mating is planned.',
    i: 'M6 3v6a6 6 0 0 0 12 0V3M6 21v-6a6 6 0 0 1 12 0v6' },
  { t: 'Vet checked and chipped', d: 'A veterinary health check and a microchip before a puppy leaves us, both dated.',
    i: 'M12 5v14M5 12h14' },
  { t: 'A written contract', d: 'A puppy purchase contract you read before anything is paid, not after.',
    i: 'M7 3h7l5 5v13H7zM14 3v5h5M10 13h6M10 17h4' },
];

// THE THIRTEEN FAQ ROWS THE RECORD NAMES, BY ID, in the record's order. Eight of them carry
// the migrated page's own questions word for word (rule 15) — four the migrated body marked up
// as keyword H3s and four from its accordion — and five are the outline's, two of them sourced
// here. The answers are data, not page copy.
const faqSection = record.sections.find((s) => s.id === 'questions')!;
const faqRows = loadFaq();
const faqs = faqSection.tree.map((n) => {
  const row = faqRows.find((r) => r.id === n.heading);
  if (!row) throw new Error(`buy-staffy-puppies-for-sale-uk: data/faq.json has no row ${n.heading}`);
  return row;
});

// The carried wording, read off the record rather than retyped (see the rule 15 note above).
// `heading` is the approved heading — already the repaired one where `verbatim.changed` says
// so — `opening` is the first paragraph the section carries word for word, and `node` is the
// same pair one level down, for the keyword H3s the migrated body put under an H2. All five
// readers are `src/lib/recordText.ts`, shared with the listing and the price page.
const { sec, heading, opening, node, nodeOpening } = recordText(record);
// The puppies section's eyebrow counts the reasons above it and the dogs beside it. Both are
// DERIVED — the record's reason nodes and data/puppies.json — so a reason added on the board
// or a puppy added to the list moves the sentence instead of leaving it wrong.
const reasonCount = (sec('reasons').tree ?? []).length;
const litterCount = (puppiesJson as PuppyRow[]).length;
const cap = (w: string) => w.charAt(0).toUpperCase() + w.slice(1);

// EVERY FIGURE THIS PAGE PRINTS IS COUNTED HERE, and the record's `n` is the expectation it is
// counted against — the lesson da9c34e wrote down, now `countedFigures()`. The record's `n` is
// a hand-written number: true on the day it was boarded, and the first thing to go stale when
// a puppy is reserved or a screen is added to the health board. So each figure is derived from
// the file its `source` names, and a count that no longer matches throws at build.
const dnaTests = healthRecord.sections.find((s) => s.id === 'dna-tests')!.table!.rows.length;
// A figure made of MORE than one fact cites more than one path (amendment 10.5), so its key is
// the whole list joined by `sourceKey()`: citing only the minimum would leave the maximum
// unsourced while reading as sourced.
const DELIVERY_SOURCES = ['data/settings.json#delivery_min_gbp', 'data/settings.json#delivery_max_gbp'];
const COUNTED: Record<string, string> = {
  'data/boards/blue-staffy-health-uk.json#len(sections[dna-tests].table.rows)': String(dnaTests),
  'data/puppies.json#len': String((puppiesJson as PuppyRow[]).length),
  [sourceKey(DELIVERY_SOURCES)]: `£${settings.delivery_min_gbp}–£${settings.delivery_max_gbp}`,
};
const counted = countedFigures(COUNTED, 'buy-staffy-puppies-for-sale-uk');

const heroSection = sec('top');
const heroChips = (heroSection.hero!.chips as LedgeEntry[]).map(ledgeText);
const heroTicks = (heroSection.hero!.ticks as LedgeEntry[]).map(ledgeText);
const counterStats = sec('stats').stats!.map(counted);

const sections = sectionsFromRecord(record);

// Each section's approved arrangement, resolved through the same `boxClass()` the board
// preview called: what the breeder signed off is what ships.
const style = (id: string) => pickedStyle(record, id);
const box = (id: string) => boxClass(style(id));
const heroStyle = style('top');
const counterStyle = style('stats');
const videoStyle = style('video-why-us');
const ownersStyle = style('owners');
const video = sec('video-why-us').video!;

// "Mo-Su 09:00-23:00" as a sentence, from the setting rather than typed as prose.
const hours = SITE.hours.replace('Mo-Su ', 'from ').replace('-', ' to ');
const town = SITE.location_label.split(' · ')[0];

// The record's schema plan: WebPage (BaseLayout) + FAQPage, and NO offer of any kind
// (`brief.schema.offer_model: "none"`). The FAQPage node is built from the SAME thirteen rows
// the accordion renders; data/faq.json keeps the sentence-case wording, which is what `name`
// reads, and the visible question is cased at render (amendment 6g). No `dateModified` here on
// purpose — BaseLayout adds the WebPage node with the git-derived dates.
const pageSchema = [
  // The VideoObject(s) for the embed(s) this page carries, built from the record's own
  // `video` block through `src/lib/video.ts` — one id, one spelling, shared with the video
  // sitemap. No `uploadDate`: no file in this repo holds one and rule 9 forbids inventing a
  // date (Known Issue 17).
  videoObject(video, abs(path)),
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'FAQPage',
    '@id': `${abs(path)}#faq`,
    mainEntity: faqs.map((r) => ({
      '@type': 'Question',
      name: r.q,
      acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: r.a },
    })),
  },
];
---
<PageShell
  title={title}
  description={description}
  canonical={path}
  ogType="article"
  schema={pageSchema}
  sections={sections}
>
  {/* 01 top — hero, picked style H-FS2 (a full-bleed photograph above the copy, the trust
      chips under the lede). The ledge is `chips`, so the record's ticks and figures are handed
      over and the arrangement is what decides they do not render there; the three figures are
      read on the counter two sections down and the delivery band is stated nowhere else in
      this page's prose. No CTA buttons (amendment 6a). The photograph is the migrated page's
      own primaryImageOfPage at its original path and alt. The H2 under the hero and its
      paragraph are the migrated wording, minus the Staffordshire Bull Terrier Club membership
      no file on disk records (verbatim.changed). */}
  <section slot="hero" id="top" data-section-label="Why families choose us" class={box('top')}>
    <Hero
      as="h1"
      {/* ONE SENTENCE, because the desktop lede is `-webkit-line-clamp: 2` and a clamp HIDES
          its overflow — a third line disappears rather than pushing anything past the ceiling,
          so the defect is invisible on the page and only a measurement finds it. The four
          things this page evidences are named in the paragraph under the H2 below, which is
          not clamped. */}
      eyebrow={`KC registered · ${SITE.location_label}`}
      title={T(h1)}
      lede="I am Lisa Bright, and this page sets out what stands behind one of our puppies."
      image={heroPhoto.file}
      imageAlt={heroPhoto.alt}
      imageWidth={heroPhoto.w}
      imageHeight={heroPhoto.h}
      layout={heroStyle.layout.hero ?? 'bleed'}
      align={heroStyle.layout.align ?? 'left'}
      media={heroStyle.layout.media ?? 'top'}
      ledge={heroStyle.layout.ledge ?? 'chips'}
      chips={heroChips}
      ticks={heroTicks}
    />
    <h2>{T(heading('top'))}</h2>
    <p>{opening('top')}</p>
    <p>
      Four things stand behind a puppy from us, and this page sets out each one:
      both parents DNA tested for L-2-HGA and HC-HSF4, a litter registered with the Kennel
      Club, a puppy reared in our own house, and the paperwork that goes home with them.
      <a href="/blue-staffy-pup-sale-uk/">What a puppy costs, and what the deposit covers</a> is
      on the price page, and
      <a href="/buy-blue-staffy-puppies-uk/">see the puppies we have for sale right now</a> on
      the listing.
      <a href="#enquiry">Ask us about any of the four</a> whenever you like.
    </p>
  </section>

  {/* 02 video-why-us — video, picked style S3 (a click-to-play facade: the thumbnail and a
      play button, with the player fetched on the first press). Working rule 14: the id is
      `g88qOo9C94c`, the one id data/facts records for this page, carried unchanged and in the
      place the migrated body put it — directly below the opening, before the reasons. */}
  <section id="video-why-us" data-section-label="The puppies themselves, on film" class={box('video-why-us')}>
    <div class="bl-head">
      <h2>{T(heading('video-why-us'))}</h2>
      <p class="bl-lede">
        A short clip of our blue Staffy puppies, with no commentary: the dogs this page is about.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="bl-body">
      <VideoEmbed
        id={video.id}
        title={video.title}
        caption={video.caption}
        play={videoStyle.layout.play ?? 'facade'}
      />
      <p>
        The case for us is made in writing below, with a document under each line; the film is
        here so you can see the puppies. The player loads only when you press it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* 03 promises — trust, picked style S2 (the strip in a card, the heading as an eyebrow),
      carrying the migrated photograph of the pups ready for collection at its original path
      and alt. The H2 and its opening are the migrated wording, minus the Assured Breeder
      sentence dropped.creds strikes. No percentage and no rating appears here. */}
  <section id="promises" data-section-label="What we can put in front of you" class={box('promises')}>
    <div class="bl-head">
      <p class="bl-eyebrow">The evidence, not the adjective</p>
      <h2>{T(heading('promises'))}</h2>
      <p class="bl-lede">{opening('promises')}</p>
    </div>
    <div class="bl-body">
      <TrustStrip items={PROMISED} />
      <div class="bl-prose">
        <img
          class="bl-img"
          src={norwichPups.file}
          alt={norwichPups.alt}
          width={norwichPups.w}
          height={norwichPups.h}
          loading="lazy"
          decoding="async"
        />
        <div class="bl-stub">
          <p>
            Four things stand behind that: both parents' DNA screening, the
            registration paperwork, the veterinary health check and microchip record, and a
            written puppy purchase contract.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* 04 stats — the counter strip, picked style C-FS2 (ring tiles in a card beside the
      heading, each label under its figure). The three figures are the record's own sourced
      rows and all three are DERIVED at build from the files they cite — the health board's
      test table, the length of our puppy list and the two delivery settings — and checked
      against the number the breeder approved. */}
  <section id="stats" data-section-label="What stands behind the puppies" class={box('stats')}>
    <div class="bl-head">
      <p class="bl-eyebrow">Read straight from our files</p>
      <h2>{T(heading('stats'))}</h2>
      <p class="bl-lede">
        The three things we can show you a file for, before you read a word of the rest.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="bl-body">
      <CounterStrip
        stats={counterStats}
        tiles={counterStyle.layout.tiles ?? 'ring'}
        label={counterStyle.layout.label ?? 'under'}
      />
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* 05 reasons — takeaways, picked style S2 (three cards across on the steel band, the
      heading as an eyebrow), carrying the migrated photograph of the English blue Staffy pup
      at its original path and alt. SEVEN InfoCards, because seven is what the body
      substantiates: the migrated meta title promised seven trusted reasons and the body listed
      five ticks, of which the price band is wrong (Known Issue 11) and "lifelong family
      support" has no term behind it. Five of the seven card headings are migrated ticks
      carried word for word, minus the tick glyph, two of them repaired in
      `verbatim.changed`. */}
  <section id="reasons" data-section-label="Seven reasons, and what backs each one" class={box('reasons')}>
    <div class="bl-head">
      <p class="bl-eyebrow">One sentence, and the file behind it</p>
      <h2>{T(heading('reasons'))}</h2>
      <p class="bl-lede">Each attached to the test, the record or the contract it rests on.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="bl-body">
      <div class="bl-cards">
        <InfoCard
          kind="fact"
          heading={T(node('reasons', 0).heading)}
          body="Both parents and the litter are registered with the Kennel Club, and a puppy travelling to you goes by DEFRA-approved transport. The credential and the carriage are kept apart, because only one of them is ours."
        />
        <InfoCard
          kind="fact"
          heading={T(node('reasons', 1).heading)}
          {/* Not "…and every puppy has a veterinary health check before it leaves us": that is
              the closing clause of data/faq.json's `about-health-tested`, which
              /blue-staffy-uk-breeders/ renders, and the two shared a twelve-word run. */}
          body="Before any mating is considered, both parents are screened by DNA for L-2-HGA and HC-HSF4, and a vet examines each puppy in the days before collection."
        />
        <InfoCard
          kind="fact"
          heading={T(node('reasons', 2).heading)}
          body="The parents, then the tests, then the contract and the records — in that order, and all of it before any money changes hands."
        />
        <InfoCard
          kind="fact"
          heading={T(node('reasons', 3).heading)}
          body={`Write to ${SITE.email} and we read and answer ${hours} every day. Feeding, the second vaccination, training, behaviour: those are the questions we get, and they are the ones we answer.`}
        />
        <InfoCard
          kind="fact"
          heading={T(node('reasons', 4).heading)}
          body="Health-tested parents, a family house, a written contract and no claim this site cannot evidence. The ethics are the list of things we will show you."
        />
        <InfoCard
          kind="fact"
          heading={T(node('reasons', 5).heading)}
          body="Every reason above names the document you can check before you travel, or the test whose paperwork follows once you ask."
        />
        <InfoCard
          kind="fact"
          heading={T(node('reasons', 6).heading)}
          body={`No rating and no percentage. We hold no document for either, and a reason we cannot evidence is not a reason. Our ${guaranteeLabel('lower')} is stated further down this page.`}
        />
      </div>
      <div class="bl-prose">
        <img
          class="bl-img"
          src={englishPup.file}
          alt={englishPup.alt}
          width={englishPup.w}
          height={englishPup.h}
          loading="lazy"
          decoding="async"
        />
        <div class="bl-stub">
          <p>
            <a href="/uk-blue-staffy-puppy-buying-guide/">Put our own buying-guide questions to us</a> rather
            than read the list. We would rather be asked than believed.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <h4>{T('Why Seven And Not Five')}</h4>
      <p>
        The old page sold seven and listed five, and two of the five cannot be carried: the
        price band it quoted is below what we charge, and an open-ended support promise has no
        end date and no file behind it. The seven here are the ones we can produce paper for.
      </p>
      <h5>{T('Each Card Names Its Own Evidence')}</h5>
      <p>A reason that could not name one would be an adjective, and it is not on the list.</p>
      <h6>{T('Reason Note: Ask for any of the seven')}</h6>
      <p>
        <a href="#enquiry">Tell us what you would like to see</a> and we will bring that
